id: ops-braces-audit
title: Remove the unpatched braces chain with built-in fs.glob and jscpd 5 only
description: "Replace fast-glob with stable Node filesystem glob discovery while preserving configured scope, dotfiles, ignores, symlink exclusions and deterministic paths. Remove the jscpd4 alias and its programmatic API/parity tests; require jscpd >=5.0.0 <6.0.0. Consumers remove their fast-glob devDependency after upgrading. The orchestrator supersedes the former jscpd4-retention requirement."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: dependencies,security
created_at: "2026-10-04T10:51:17.651Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T06:31:29.970Z"
author: codex-sol
repro_steps: npm ci; npm audit; npm ls braces; npm view braces version
resolution: Replace npm fast-glob discovery with Node built-ins; remove jscpd4 support and its dependency chain; retain jscpd 5 real-engine tests and all 100% coverage thresholds. Consumers remove fast-glob after the released upgrade. Native Bun negative-extglob parity is tracked separately.
expected_result: "Both npm audit variants report zero vulnerabilities, npm ls braces is empty, npm and Bun release checks retain all 100% thresholds, and packed duplication gates run without fast-glob."
actual_result: Candidate npm audit and npm audit --omit=dev each report 0 vulnerabilities; npm ls braces and npm ls fast-glob are empty. Six filesystem contracts pass against both original and replacement matchers; all 25 focused Node tests and four packed npm/native Bun clean/duplicate scenarios pass.
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T04:26:33.307Z",codex-agent,"The orchestrator supersedes the old prohibition on removing the jscpd4 alias: jscpd 5 only is now required. Plan: pin existing filesystem glob semantics before replacing fast-glob with stable Node fs.glob, remove both vulnerable dependency sources, preserve 100% thresholds, and verify npm/Bun release and packed consumers without fast-glob."
  "2026-10-14T04:31:38.087Z",codex-agent,"Baseline: npm ci reports 5 high vulnerabilities; npm audit --omit=dev reports 0. Four filesystem contract tests pass on the original fast-glob matcher before replacement. Native glob requires compatibility handling for dotfiles and brace-union negative patterns; these are pinned by the tests."
  "2026-10-14T04:43:42.152Z",codex-agent,"Discovery preserves explicit symlink bases and paths outside the repo root, with six filesystem contracts verified against the original fast-glob function first. Node native glob and path.matchesGlob replace npm glob dependencies; hidden-entry supplementation and lstat avoid Bun fs.glob limitations. Consumer follow-up after release: delete fast-glob devDependency and refresh lockfiles in pm-web, pm-graph, pm-gantt-chart, pm-jev, pm-lint, pm-review, pm-slack-standup and pm-ts-starter."
  "2026-10-14T04:44:40.562Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural proof: the same six filesystem tests pass on the original fast-glob matcher and on the restored built-in matcher. In disposable copies changing only globMatchedSources, omitting hidden includes or removing canonical ignores causes pinned tests to fail. No coverage threshold changed."
  "2026-10-14T04:47:10.999Z",codex-agent,"Runtime boundary: all six scope contracts pass on Node; native Bun default-glob packed gates pass, but Bun 1.3.5 path.matchesGlob rejects the negative-extglob control. Tracked as ops-bun-negative-extglobs. Documented consumer launchers invoke Node. Full release gates retain two existing opt-in live-fleet skips when PM_OPS_TEST_REPOS is unset; this PR does not certify live fleet state."
  "2026-10-14T05:04:40.323Z",codex-agent,"Final candidate gates: env -u PM_PATH -u PM_AUTHOR HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check and the same with bun run release:check both passed: 717 tests, 715 passed, 0 failed/cancelled/todo, 2 existing opt-in live-fleet skips. Coverage: 100% statements, branches, functions and lines across 25 source files; docstrings: 232 declarations across 25 files; duplication: 61 sources, 0 clone pairs, 0%. Both npm audits report 0 vulnerabilities; braces and fast-glob dependency trees are empty. Node 22.19 focused tests: 25/25 passed. Both linked commands pass together, including four packed npm/native Bun clean/duplicate scenarios. Behavioural proof: original and restored matchers 6/6; hidden-include mutation 4 failures; ignore mutation 5 failures. No PM CLI/SDK bump or threshold change. pm test injects npm allow-scripts configuration rejected by project installs; the disposable packed fixture clears it. Known native Bun negative-extglob limitation remains in ops-bun-negative-extglobs; requested publish-wrapper issue is ops-third-party-publish-wrappers. Consumer upgrades remain follow-up after release."
  "2026-10-14T05:21:52.342Z",pi-agent,"CodeQL js/polynomial-redos alert #18 on the brace-union regex introduced by this PR: the leftmost-union exec() backtracks polynomially, and measurements confirm it (adversarial '{{,' + 50k commas takes ~19.4 s; the 200k variant exceeds 100 s). Plan: replace the regex with a single-pass indexOf/char scanner that keeps the exact leftmost expandable-union semantics (nested and non-comma braces untouched, same left-to-right expansion order), bound expansion at 1024 alternatives with a clear refusal error so hostile configured globs cannot explode memory, document the limit in the docstring and README, add adversarial timing, expansion-limit and semantics tests, and record a behavioural revert proof."
  "2026-10-14T05:27:21.829Z",pi-agent,"Revert proof (behavioural): with only expandGlobUnions restored to the flagged regex body, the new tests fail exactly as required — the adversarial timing test takes 20.6 s (50 ms bound; the 200k-comma variant exceeds 100 s) and the expansion-refusal test fails because the unbounded regex silently expands past 1024 alternatives. With the linear scanner restored, the same suite passes: the '{{,' + 50k-commas input expands in ~0.2 ms and the closing-brace variant refuses in ~0.3 ms. Semantics were also differentially verified: the scanner and the old regex produce identical expansions for 400,000 random patterns (including nested, non-comma, empty-alternative and negative-alternative braces)."
  "2026-10-14T06:03:55.650Z",pi-agent,"CodeQL fix gates (isolated identity, no PM_PATH/PM_AUTHOR, scratch HOME, no git config): npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0 with identical counts — 720 tests, 718 passed, 0 failed/cancelled/todo, 2 existing opt-in live-fleet skips (3 new brace-union tests added to the previous 717/715). Coverage 100% statements, branches, functions and lines across 25 source files; docstrings 235 declarations across 25 files; duplication gate 0% duplicated lines (0/25281), 62 sources, 0 clone pairs; changelog check passes unchanged after changelog:full. dist/ rebuilt with the repo build (tsc). Adversarial timing: '{{,' + 50k commas now expands in about 0.2 ms and the closing-brace variant refuses in about 0.3 ms, versus 19.4 s / >100 s with the flagged regex."
  "2026-10-14T06:31:29.970Z",claude-hub,"Review round 1 (CodeRabbit, PR #163 head 41125c7): the 50 ms wall-clock bound in the linear-time ReDoS test could fail on a loaded runner or under c8 coverage without a real regression. The bound is now 1 s. The polynomial regex took ~19 s on this input and the scanner takes ~1-6 ms, so the regression is still caught with about 150x margin."
files[7]{path,scope,note}:
  duplication.ts,project,"Linear single-pass brace-union scanner replacing the polynomial regex, with a 1024-alternative refusal bound"
  package.json,project,Remove fast-glob and jscpd4; require jscpd 5
  test/coverage-gate.test.ts,project,Remove the final test-only fast-glob import
  test/duplication-glob-unions.test.ts,project,"Brace-union order/literal contracts, expansion refusal bound and adversarial ReDoS timing"
  test/duplication-glob.test.ts,project,Filesystem contracts pinned on fast-glob before replacement
  test/duplication-packed.acceptance.ts,project,Packed npm and native Bun clean and duplicate gates without fast-glob or braces
  test/lint-and-duplication-gates.test.ts,project,Retain real jscpd 5 tests; remove jscpd 4 parity
tests[3]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node --test test/duplication-glob.test.ts test/lint-and-duplication-gates.test.ts,project,codex-agent,"2026-10-14T04:33:55.291Z",local_mutation,fix/braces-free-duplication-gate
  node test/duplication-packed.acceptance.ts,project,codex-agent,"2026-10-14T04:49:37.495Z",local_mutation,fix/braces-free-duplication-gate
  node --test test/duplication-glob-unions.test.ts test/duplication-glob.test.ts,project,pi-agent,"2026-10-14T05:28:32.577Z",local_mutation,fix/braces-free-duplication-gate
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  README.md,project,Document linear brace expansion and the 1024-alternative refusal bound
